

Introduction:
The retail and e-commerce industry generates large volumes of transactional data from product sales, customer purchases, and inventory movements. 
Organizations often struggle to transform this raw data into actionable insights that support strategic decision-making. Business Intelli-gence dashboards and 
analytical tools play a crucial role in helping organizations monitor prod-uct performance, identify revenue drivers, and optimize product portfolios.
This project presents the development of a Coffee Roasters Sales Performance Dashboard, built using Python, Streamlit, SQLite, and Plotly. The dashboard 
consolidates sales and product performance data into an interactive analytics platform that enables users to evaluate revenue trends, product contribution, 
category performance, and revenue concentration. The applica-tion includes modules such as Product KPI Monitoring, Pareto Analysis, Category Distribution Analysis, 
ABC Classification, and Product Portfolio Analysis.
From a business perspective, the dashboard demonstrates how data visualization and analytics can improve decision-making by identifying high-performing products, 
understanding cus-tomer purchasing patterns, and highlighting products that contribute most significantly to over-all revenue. The project transforms complex 
transactional data into intuitive visualizations that support both operational monitoring and strategic planning.

